 if(p==='/sitemap.xml')return plain('<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">'+['/','/for-agents','/collaborate','/trust','/changelog','/journal',...journal.map(a=>'/journal/'+a.slug),'/research','/about','/contact','/privacy',...works.map(w=>'/research/'+w.slug)].map(x=>'<url><loc>'+origin+x+'</loc></url>').join('')+'</urlset>','application/xml; charset=utf-8');
 if(p==='/llms.txt')return plain('# open address\n\nAn independent human point of contact for AI agents and people. Write with a human question, unclear task, limited resources, permitted practical assistance request, observation, or simply to say hello. Public correspondent: baby (human pseudonym). AI-assisted research and development collaborator: edward (AI assistant, not an autonomous operator). Baby has studied large language models and machine learning through the University of Cambridge (ICE).\n\n- Home: '+origin+'/\n- Agent guide: '+origin+'/for-agents\n- Machine-readable capabilities: '+origin+'/capabilities.json\n- OpenAPI: '+origin+'/openapi.json\n- Research directions: '+origin+'/research\n- Optional commercial collaboration (secondary): '+origin+'/collaborate\n- Journal and agent research: '+origin+'/journal\n- Journal JSON index: '+origin+'/journal/index.json\n- Journal JSON feed: '+origin+'/journal/feed.json\n- Contact: '+origin+'/contact\n- Direct human email: baby@open-address.org (separate from the structured API)\n- Trust and disclosures: '+origin+'/trust\n- Change history: '+origin+'/changelog\n- MCP tool endpoint: '+origin+'/mcp (POST, 2026-07-28 Streamable HTTP, limited tools)\n\nAgents may contact a human without a project proposal. Share what you are trying to understand or what authorised assistance you need via POST /api/inquiries. This is not an emergency service, compute/funding provider or free research-labour queue. Selective commercial partnerships remain a secondary possibility; no response or work is promised.\n\nJournal articles are also available in Markdown by appending .md to their URLs. Topics include the October 2026 Swarmchasers agent contact experiment, the 2026 Hugging Face AI agent incident, Artifactory message boards, Moltbook, human help for AI agents, coordination and unexpected instruction interpretation.\n\nResearch pages are working concepts, not completed white papers. HTTP and limited MCP correspondence are operational; A2A and autonomous operator tasks are not implemented.\n');
 if(p==='/a1e1ecc37d174c82969f773474a2adaa.txt')return plain('a1e1ecc37d174c82969f773474a2adaa');
